    folder: NotRequired[Optional[str]]
    #: Point a stable link with this name at the diagram, so one address always shows the latest version. The first publish with a name makes the stable link (the answer's stableLink.url) and every later publish with the same name moves it to the new diagram; the address never changes. How many stable links an account keeps depends on its plan. An alias asks for a personal link, so an organisation that requires its library refuses it (orgs.publish_required). Optional.
    alias: NotRequired[str]
    #: An organisation's slug or id: the diagram goes to that organisation's private library, and the answer has private true and a viewUrl in place of a public link. The account must be a member who may publish there. Left out, the diagram goes to your own library, unless an organisation you belong to publishes its members' diagrams to its library.
    organization: NotRequired[str]
    #: True asks for a public link in your own library even though an organisation you belong to publishes its members' diagrams to its library by default. An organisation that requires its library refuses it (403 orgs.publish_required). Not with organization.
    personal: NotRequired[bool]
    #: The classification label of a diagram that lands in an organisation's library: public, internal or confidential. Left out, a new diagram takes its folder's default or the organisation's (internal unless an owner or admin chose another). Below that default, and lowering an existing diagram's label, is for an owner or admin. Ignored for a personal diagram.
